WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.438 --> 00:00:04.504
-The Biden administration moved
to oust several Trump holdovers,

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.439
including Sean Spicer and
Kellyanne Conway,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.840
from military academy boards,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.609
while the former president
himself

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.977
issued a statement claiming

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.279
that -- let me see
if I have this right --

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.748
Confederate General
Robert E. Lee

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.583
would have won
the war in Afghanistan.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.885
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:23.356
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.658
There's a simple truth
about our history

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.693
which has somehow been muddied
through decades

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:30.597
of self-serving revisionism by
racists and apologists

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.699
for white supremacy,
and that is that the Confederacy

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.736
was a movement of anti-American
traders and slavers

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.304
who tried to destroy
this country.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.807
I can't believe that even
has to be said,

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.075
but, apparently, it does.
There are people out there

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.044
who don't even know
what the Civil War was about,

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.947
like, for example, the former
president of the United States.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:52.818
-People don't realize, you know,
the Civil War, um...

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:56.188
-Yeah.
-...you think about it, why?

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.358
People don't ask that question,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.526
but why was there the Civil War?

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:03.029
Why could that one
not have been worked out?

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.665
-Yeah, people
don't ask the question

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.301
"Why was there the Civil War?"
just like we don't ask,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.470
"How many sides
does a triangle have?"

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.272
or, "Is a snake a reptile?"

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.640
Because we learned all that
[Bleep] in grade school.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.609
At least, those of us
who weren't following our dad

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.811
to construction sites
to watch him yell at immigrants.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.647
What do you mean
"don't ask that question"?

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.382
It was a white-supremacist
rebellion

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.851
against the government,
not a fight between

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.787
my wife and her sister.
"What are they mad about?"

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.088
"Don't ask."

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.657
I know Donald Trump doesn't live
in our reality,

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.760
but it's still interesting
to find out stuff

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.495
about his reality.
Like, I guess, in his reality,

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.964
the local libraries only have
one book on the Civil War,

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:42.101
called, "What the Heck Was All
This Nonsense About?"

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.636
Also, I like
that he wants to know

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.039
why could that not have
been worked out?

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.107
Yeah, why couldn't you get
the top Union generals

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.909
and the to Confederate generals
in a room,

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.177
stick Andy Cohen in the middle,

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.079
and talk it down
over some skinny margs?

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.880
I mean, seriously,
you don't have to be

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.382
the chair of a college
history department

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:59.285
to know that the Confederacy
and its leaders were evil.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.120
Hell, you just had to have
a substitute teacher

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.655
in high school
who forgot the lesson plan

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.090
and played "Glory" on laser disc

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.325
while he put his head down
on the desk and took a nap.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.795
Yeah, sure, sure,
all the other kids

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.230
secretly passed notes
and played games,

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.500
but me, I was watching.
Total "Glory" stand.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.936
You might say
that for one magical year,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.270
I was deep in the "Glory" hole.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.006
I'd prefer if you didn't!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:24.644
Come on, Freeman, Washington,
Braugher, yes, please.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.645
Plus, I like to pretend that
Matthew Broderick's character

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:29.249
was just like Ferris Bueller,
and before every battle,

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.785
the general would say,
"Colonel Shaw?

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.888
Colonel Shaw?"

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.123
Unfortunately, part of the
reason we have to keep stating

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:41.427
that obvious fact about
the evil of the Confederacy

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.429
and the reality of
the Civil War is

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.031
that shortly after
the end of the war,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.567
in Reconstruction,
a racist revisionist

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.235
lost-cause movement rose up

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.404
to cast the leaders
of the Confederacy

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.340
as a noble gentleman,
instead of the defeated traders

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.775
and white supremacists
that they were.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.644
Nowadays, lots of us don't even
learn about Reconstruction

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:01.114
and the post-Civil War period
in history class.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.781
I mean, I can't believe
people are worried

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:04.216
about critical race theory

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:05.451
when my history textbook

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.453
jumped from the Civil War
to the Great Depression,

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.156
and in between, there was one
page about William Howard Taft

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.223
getting stuck in a bathtub.

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.025
Now, I know
that story is apocryphal,

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.361
and that it didn't even start
to spread until decades later,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.996
but it's also super funny to me

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.564
that someone
went out of their way

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.900
to make it up and spread it
around about a dead guy.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.402
I mean, Taft was the only person
in American history

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:25.838
to ever serve as
president and chief justice,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.407
and yet all anyone knows
about him

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:30.342
is a fake story that sounds like
a plot line from "Family Guy."

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:33.346
"Oh, Lois, it happened again.
Get the jaws of life."

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:36.148
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:38.518
"Raymond?"
"No!"

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.919
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.654
"Peter!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:45.057
And that's why there was a giant
statue of Robert E. Lee

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.893
on a horse looming over
the old capital

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.496
of the Confederacy in Richmond
for 130 years

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.199
because white supremacists and
Confederacy apologists

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.501
tried to recast him
as some sort of noble hero,

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.304
even though it was known
at the time

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.973
by actual Civil War heroes
that Lee was a traitor

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.509
who disgraced himself.
Ulysses S. Grant said

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.045
the cause Lee fought for
"was, I believe,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.113
one of the worst for which
a people ever fought,

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:10.549
and one for which there was
the least excuse."

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:13.086
And Grant's
the guy who beat Lee.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.988
How the hell did Lee end up with
a giant statue, and not Grant?

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.024
If anything, there should have
been a giant statue in Richmond

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.693
of Grant kicking Lee
in the balls.

00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:24.296
Even better, it could be
a clock that tolls on the hour.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:27.400
[ Bell tolls ]

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.637
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.906
Not sure if 1:00 was
the funniest of our options.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.874
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:38.477
Well, yesterday, finally,
after 130 years,

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:40.546
that wretched monument
to an evil cause

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.915
was finally taken down,
with a crowd gathering

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.351
to celebrate
as Lee was hauled away.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.719
-The nation's largest
Confederate monument

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:49.521
just came down.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:52.324
The giant Robert E. Lee statue
in Richmond, Virginia,

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.461
which is 6 stories tall and
weighs 12 tons,

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.795
well, it was just removed.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:59.198
Shaq, what is the community
saying about this?

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.535
What was it like to watch this?

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:05.672
-I'll tell you,
there were celebrations,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.140
there were cheers,
there were chants.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.611
-♪ Na-na-na na,
na-na-na na ♪

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:17.183
♪ Hey, hey, goodbye ♪

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.651
-First of all,
as a baseball fan,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.320
I love the crowd taunting him
like he's a Yankees reliever

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.723
in Fenway who just got pulled
after coughing up six runs

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.990
in the bottom of the eighth.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.025
There should have been
an angry Sox fan there

00:05:27.025 --> 00:05:28.694
pouring beer on his head.

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.662
Also, as someone who grew up
going to Fenway,

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:33.098
I can attest that Red Sox fans
are unruly, drunk, and

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.868
yet surprisingly knowledgeable
about history.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.569
"Hit the showers, Bobby,

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:40.373
and then go take your medicine
at Appomattox!"

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.341
Yeah, that's right,
the Yankees are the new Mets

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:44.243
in "Closer Look" punch lines,
gut don't worry,

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.145
the Mets blew it
in extra innings last night,

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.546
so they're still the Mets.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:50.283
I don't follow the Mets scores.
I just know what happened

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.750
because as I was leaving
last night,

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.486
the entire crew was sitting
in a circle,

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:55.922
sobbing and hugging each other,
and saying,

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.257
"We don't deserve this,"
which just between us,

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:01.160
some of them do.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.362
Second, there's
nothing more humiliating

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:07.366
than being carried away
on a horse, in the air.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:09.001
When you're sitting astride
a horse on the ground,

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.169
you look like a noble hero,

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.871
but when you're sitting
on one in the sky,

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.839
getting lifted up by a crane,
you look like

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.041
a Porta-Potty getting hauled
away after Burning Man

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.477
or a guy who glued himself
to his horse

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.379
and now can't get
out the front door.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.448
"Oh, it happened again."
"Raymond?"

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.849
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:25.851
Anyone who loves America
should be watching this scene

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.352
and celebrating
along with the crowd.

00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:29.489
A monument to a traitor
who fought for an evil cause --

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:31.724
the cause of slavery --
white supremacy,

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:33.258
and who tried to destroy
the United States

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:35.127
finally has been taken down,
but you'll never guess

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:36.529
who had a slightly different
take on things.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.797
-Former President Donald Trump
issued a statement

00:06:38.797 --> 00:06:41.634
calling the removal a, quote,
"complete desecration"

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.003
and lamenting that Lee
was not available

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:46.505
to lead the United States
in Afghanistan.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:49.542
-Trump said in a statement,
quote, "If only we had

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.243
Robert E. Lee
to command our troops

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.746
in Afghanistan,
that disaster would have ended

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.582
in a complete and total victory
many years ago.

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.751
What an embarrassment
we are suffering

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:02.722
because we don't have
the genius of a Robert E. Lee!"

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.856
-First of all, dingus,
you're from Queens.

00:07:04.856 --> 00:07:07.259
It's pretty hard to remake
yourself as a good old boy

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:08.961
when you sound like
a super in Astoria.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.762
"You know what this [Bleep]
apartment needs?

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:13.466
Some freakin' magnolias.
Oh!"

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:15.268
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:18.070
Seriously, what do you mean
it would have ended in victory

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.805
if Lee was in charge?
He lost.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:22.007
He's famous for losing.
But, ah, yes,

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:24.710
if only Robert E. Lee had been
in charge in Afghanistan,

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.979
then surely he would have said
something inspirational,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.480
like, "Is that a missile?!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.449
All I have is a bayonet,
and I'm glued to my horse!

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:33.051
Get me out of here!"
Trump also called it

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:34.787
"a beautiful piece
of bronze sculpture."

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.822
And if Trump ever calls anything
beautiful,

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.058
you know it's the opposite.
Look at his apartment.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:42.528
It looks like the set of an '80s
game show called "Gold Rush."

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.264
Of course, I wouldn't recommend
taking history lessons

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.699
from a guy who,
among other things,

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.634
praised Nazis,
sowed an insurrection

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.569
where rioters carried
the Confederate flag,

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:52.772
thought Frederick Douglass
was still alive,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:55.240
didn't know why the Civil War
happened in the first place,

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.978
and thought there were airports
during the Revolutionary War.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:03.616
-The Continental Army suffered a
bitter winter of Valley Forge,

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:06.351
found glory across the waters
of the Delaware,

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:10.355
and seized victory
from Cornwallis of Yorktown.

00:08:10.355 --> 00:08:15.661
Our Army manned the airports --
rammed the ramparts,

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:19.532
it took over the airports,
it did everything it had to do.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.266
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:22.368
-That's right.
Who can forget

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:23.869
the infamous
Battle of LaGuardia,

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:25.671
where Patrick Henry
famously said,

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:28.708
"Give me priority boarding
or give me death"?

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.876
"He's why the peanuts
are free now.

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:34.413
Used to have to pay
for the peanuts."

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.749
To this day, schoolchildren
still take trips

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.684
to the Buffalo Wild Wings
in Terminal D,

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:41.353
where Washington's army
camped out during the winter.

00:08:41.353 --> 00:08:42.755
And we all remember the words

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.857
of British general
Charles Cornwallis,

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:47.292
who upon surrendering, said, "We
just want to leave LaGuardia.

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:50.763
Where is ground transportation?
The signs are very confusing."

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:53.599
This is the guy the Republican
Party has made its leader --

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.868
the guy they've lined up behind,
a guy who sowed an insurrection

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.103
to overthrow democracy,
oversaw the preventable death

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.338
of hundreds of thousands
of people,

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.473
and praised
traitors and racists.

00:09:01.473 --> 00:09:03.743
That's why he and his loyalists
need to be thoroughly banished

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:05.677
from our institutions and
shunned from our politics.

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:06.979
And yesterday
the Biden administration

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:09.849
took another small step toward
accomplishing that goal.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:11.484
-Months into
Joe Biden's presidency,

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.486
his administration is still
cleaning house

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:15.287
as it relates to
former Trump officials,

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:16.789
with the director
of the White House's

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:19.891
presidential personnel office
sending letters to 18 people

00:09:19.891 --> 00:09:22.093
on three different
government advisory boards,

00:09:22.093 --> 00:09:23.895
asking them to resign.

00:09:23.895 --> 00:09:26.098
-Familiar names include
White House counselor

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:28.734
Kellyanne Conway
to the Air Force Academy,

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:31.703
and former press secretary
Sean Spicer

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:33.338
to the Naval Academy.

00:09:33.338 --> 00:09:35.507
-Why were there still any
Trump holdovers anyway?

00:09:35.507 --> 00:09:37.476
That's like moving into
a rent-controlled apartment

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.078
the last guy died in,
and keeping

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:41.180
all the expired whitefish
in the refrigerator.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.449
And why was Kellyanne Conway
on an Air Force advisory board?

00:09:44.449 --> 00:09:48.387
If she ever flew an F-16 or what
she probably calls an F-17,

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:50.189
guessing it would end up
in a ravine,

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:51.991
with her standing on the tarmac
in a parachute,

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.993
claiming it was
a successful landing.

00:09:53.993 --> 00:09:55.661
"The plane is on the ground.

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:57.062
Do you not think the plane
is on the ground?"

00:09:57.062 --> 00:09:59.065
But my favorite part
of this little episode was

00:09:59.065 --> 00:10:01.767
the reaction from former Trump
press secretary Sean Spicer,

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:04.203
a commander in the
U.S. Naval Reserve

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:06.972
who apparently has his own show
on Newsmax now.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:10.309
Spicer was outraged by the
explanation for his removal

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:13.179
given know by current White
House press secretary Jen Psaki.

00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:14.580
First, let's see Psaki's answer.

00:10:23.655 --> 00:10:25.991
-Well, I will let others
